      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-STARTER-007` Byte-Coin x2: Crypto. `+2 Crypto.` Cost 3.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-STARTER-008",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-STARTER-008` Kilo-Coin x1: Crypto. `+3 Crypto.` Cost 6.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-ACTION-001",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-ACTION-001` Turn 1 grants +2 Actions, Turn 2 +1, Turn 3 +1.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-ACTION-002",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-ACTION-002` No maximum Action capacity.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-ACTION-003",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-ACTION-003` Action carryover between Runtime turns is configurable. Actions never carry between Cycles.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-ACTION-004",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-ACTION-004` OnReveal happens after deployment ends. Actions gained on reveal are usable on the next Runtime turn.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-001",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-001` V1 uses Runtime Mode only.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-002",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-002` Turn 1 opens Nodes 1–3. Turn 2 opens Node 4. Turn 3 opens Node 5.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-003",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-003` Runtime timers are configurable.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-004",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-004` Once open, Nodes remain legally playable until Collapse unless an approved restriction applies.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-005",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-005` Max 4 cards per player per Node unless amended by effect.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-006",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-006` Cards deploy face down. Commitments remain hidden until deployment ends.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-007",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-007` Cards at unopened Nodes remain unrevealed and ineligible until that Node opens. Original play-order information is preserved while they wait. A card played at an already-open Node is eligible for that turn's post-deployment reveal sequence.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-008",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-008` During a reveal sequence, the priority player reveals their first eligible card, then the other player reveals their first eligible card. Continue alternating while both players have eligible cards. If one player has no remaining eligible cards, the other player's remaining eligible cards reveal in their own play order. Example when Player A has reveal priority: A1 → B1 → A2 → B2 → A3 → A4.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-009",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-009` When a Node opens, unrevealed cards already there become eligible and reveal before deployment for that newly opened turn begins. That opening reveal uses original play order and the current player reveal priority / alternation.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-010",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-010` Each player's internal card order is the chronological order in which that player played their cards. Play order matters. Do not reorder a player's cards by Node number.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-011",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-011` If no legal plays remain, communicate that state and allow/require End Turn.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-012",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-012` Initial reveal priority is randomly assigned.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-013",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-013` Reveal priority is set once per Runtime turn and is not recalculated between individual reveals in that turn's sequence.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-RUNTIME-014",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-RUNTIME-014` After a Runtime turn's reveal window closes, calculate each player's controlled probability weight under `RULE-PROB-007`. The player with greater controlled probability weight receives reveal priority for the next Runtime turn. If equal, the current priority player retains it.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-POWER-001",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-POWER-001` Current Node control is represented by current total Power. Final winner is determined during Collapse.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-POWER-002",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-POWER-002` Highest value wins even if negative.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-POWER-003",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-POWER-003` Empty side counts as 0 Power.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-POWER-004",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-POWER-004` Ties split Node weight evenly. If neither player has cards, weight is also split evenly.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-POWER-005",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-POWER-005` Node Power is not a third gameplay value. It names the current Power totals of the two players at that Node: Node P1 Power and Node P2 Power. The Node winner at Collapse is determined by comparing those player totals after applicable effects and recalculation.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-PROB-001",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-PROB-001` Current initial weights: 30%, 25%, 20%, 15%, 10%, configurable.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-PROB-002",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-PROB-002` Distribution totals 100%.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-PROB-003",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-PROB-003` Redistribution must come from another Node. Probability cannot go below 0%.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-PROB-004",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-PROB-004` If transfer exceeds source amount, transfer all remaining source probability.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-PROB-005",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-PROB-005` Nodes may reach 0% or 100%.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-PROB-006",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-PROB-006` Support 0.5% increments.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-PROB-007",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`RULE-PROB-007` Controlled probability weight is the sum of current Node probability weights a player controls. A player receives the full current weight of each Node they are winning and half the current weight of each tied Node. Empty Nodes are 0 Power vs 0 Power and therefore tied. ControlledWeight(A) = Σ(weights of Nodes A is winning) + ½ Σ(weights of tied Nodes). The same applies independently to the other player. This is not raw card Power and not the Wave Collapse random selection. It determines next-turn reveal priority under `RULE-RUNTIME-014`.",
      "tags": [
        "rule"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "01_APPROVED_RULES.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "RULE-COLLAPSE-001",
      "domain": "RULE",
      "status": "current",
